      "problem": "Find $\\mathcal{P}(A)$ if $A = \\{ 2, 4, \\{ 8 \\} \\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The power set of $A,$ denoted $\\mathcal{P}(A),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $A,$ including the empty set $\\emptyset.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $A$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14180007/assets/b3af256806e0aeb0396564320800f908c66d5830ab46e676dfc51ceab24154f6.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $A$ are\n\n$$\n\\emptyset = \\{\\},\\quad \\{2\\},\\quad \\{4\\},\\quad \\{ \\{8\\} \\}, \\quad \\{2, 4\\},\\quad \\{2, \\{8\\}\\},\\quad \\{4, \\{8\\}\\},\\quad\\{2, 4, \\{8\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{P}(A) = \\{\\emptyset, \\{2\\}, \\{4\\}, \\{\\{8\\}\\}, \\{2, 4\\}, \\{2, \\{8\\}\\}, \\{4, \\{8\\}\\},\\{2, 4, \\{8\\}\\}\\}.\n$$",
